  "final_answer_preview": "The relevant offence for obstructing a public road and causing danger is outlined in Section 285 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023. This section states that anyone who causes danger, obstruction, or injury to any person in a public way through their actions or negligence can be punished with a fine of up to five thousand rupees. Additionally, Section 270 defines a public nuisance as any act or omission that causes common injury, danger, or annoyance to the public, which may also apply in this context. Furthermore, Section 281 addresses reckless or negligent driving on public ways, which could also be relevant if the obstruction involved a vehicle.",
